      "timestamp": "2026-11-18T17:42:05.817Z",
      "commits": [
        {
          "sha": "9353f597c5bfd18851f1ae05fc72ff59fd07c684",
          "author_name": "Brandon Fryslie",
          "author_email": "530235+brandon-fryslie@users.noreply.github.com",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-18T10:41:02-07:00",
          "message": "Merge 855d3bd53391b53da8c38c5ee186960a4410ff82 into fd629edab3c2116a266ec18501d1ce208592daaf\n"
        },
        {
          "sha": "855d3bd53391b53da8c38c5ee186960a4410ff82",
          "author_name": "Brandon Fryslie",
          "author_email": "530235+brandon-fryslie@users.noreply.github.com",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-18T10:39:28-07:00",
          "message": "fix(watchers): each branch refs directory is its own watch, and one that cannot be opened is the registry's refusal (pkcy)\n\nOn Linux under Node 20 and 22 a recursive fs.watch is Node's own\nwalk, which stops at an entry it cannot open and still reads as\nlistening. The git watch now names refs/heads and every directory\nbelow it, and each link there, as a plain directory target on every\npass. A directory the listing cannot open is still named, so the\nregistry refuses it, logs and counts it, and retries it each period.\nThe registry loses its recursive arm.\n"
        }
      ]
    },
